WEBVTT

1
00:00:34.035 --> 00:00:37.580
My name is Ash,
and I'm a slave.

2
00:00:40.959 --> 00:00:43.711
Close as I can figure it,
the year is 1300 A.D...

3
00:00:43.795 --> 00:00:46.422
and I'm being
dragged to my death.

4
00:00:46.506 --> 00:00:48.841
It wasn't always like this.

5
00:00:49.425 --> 00:00:52.220
I had a real life once.

6
00:00:53.429 --> 00:00:55.265
A job.

7
00:00:56.474 --> 00:00:58.601
Ash to price check four.

8
00:01:00.562 --> 00:01:03.106
Hardware, aisle 12.

9
00:01:03.189 --> 00:01:05.233
Shop smart,
shop S-mart.

10
00:01:05.316 --> 00:01:08.820
I had a wonderful girlfriend:
Linda.

11
00:01:11.614 --> 00:01:15.201
Together, we drove to
a small cabin in the mountains.

12
00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:21.749
It seems an archaeologist
had come to this remote place...

13
00:01:21.833 --> 00:01:24.752
to translate and study
his latest find:

14
00:01:25.628 --> 00:01:30.633
Necronomicon Ex Mortis,
the Book of the Dead.

15
00:01:32.385 --> 00:01:35.805
Bound in human flesh
and inked in blood...

16
00:01:35.888 --> 00:01:40.435
this ancient Sumerian text
contained bizarre burial rites...

17
00:01:40.518 --> 00:01:45.315
funerary incantations
and demon resurrection passages.

18
00:01:46.399 --> 00:01:48.943
It was never meant
for the world of the living.

19
00:01:49.527 --> 00:01:53.156
The book awoke something dark
in the woods.

20
00:01:59.329 --> 00:02:01.623
It took Linda.

21
00:02:01.706 --> 00:02:04.626
And then it came for me.

22
00:02:05.501 --> 00:02:07.837
It got into my hand
and it went bad.

23
00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:10.965
So I lopped it off
at the wrist.

24
00:02:16.554 --> 00:02:19.349
But that didn't stop it.
It came back.

25
00:02:22.018 --> 00:02:23.853
Big time.

26
00:02:40.495 --> 00:02:41.996
Oh, my God!

27
00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:44.040
How do you stop it?

28
00:03:55.445 --> 00:03:58.573
Where in the hell...?

29
00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:08.207
Stand fast, hellhound!

30
00:04:08.833 --> 00:04:11.294
No, no...
Easy now, chief.

31
00:04:12.336 --> 00:04:18.760
I don't know how I got here...
and I'm not looking for any trouble.

32
00:04:20.845 --> 00:04:22.638
What a piece of armor this is!

33
00:04:24.307 --> 00:04:28.853
- Wise man!
- Fall back! Back on your horses. Come on!

34
00:04:31.063 --> 00:04:34.859
My Lord, I believe he is the one
written of in the Necronomicon.

35
00:04:34.942 --> 00:04:37.528
He who's prophesied to fall
from the heavens...

36
00:04:37.612 --> 00:04:40.364
and deliver us
from the terrors of the Deadites.

37
00:04:40.448 --> 00:04:42.158
What? That buffoon?

38
00:04:42.241 --> 00:04:47.079
Likely...
he's one of Henry's men!

39
00:04:47.705 --> 00:04:50.625
Kneel, rapscallions!

40
00:04:51.584 --> 00:04:53.753
I say to the pit with him!

41
00:04:53.836 --> 00:04:57.965
You shall soon
learn the horrors of the pit.

42
00:04:58.049 --> 00:05:01.511
- To the pit!
- You miserable bast...

43
00:05:03.304 --> 00:05:05.181
- Get him!
- Get off of me!

44
00:05:07.058 --> 00:05:10.186
- Let me go!
- Chain him!

45
00:05:12.563 --> 00:05:15.858
Ah, you're gonna have
a little bit of wee fun, mate.

46
00:05:17.235 --> 00:05:19.195
To the castle!

47
00:05:22.114 --> 00:05:25.701
Pick up your feet!
Stop draggin' your feet! Come on!

48
00:05:25.785 --> 00:05:28.704
Move along!
Come on, now.

49
00:05:29.372 --> 00:05:32.917
Come on, pick it up.
Have a taste of this!

50
00:05:40.466 --> 00:05:42.927
You men got something
to look forward to...

51
00:05:43.010 --> 00:05:45.763
when you get back
to the castle.

52
00:05:46.472 --> 00:05:50.852
Lord Arthur approaches!
Raise the portcullis!

53
00:05:52.144 --> 00:05:56.858
Lord Arthur!
Lord Arthur approaches!

54
00:06:02.655 --> 00:06:06.951
You miserable clogs!
Don't drag thy feet!

55
00:06:08.995 --> 00:06:12.415
That's lovely, isn't it?
Move it in.

56
00:06:12.498 --> 00:06:14.792
You worthless bastards!

57
00:06:45.615 --> 00:06:50.369
Lord Arthur, where is my brother?
Did he not ride with you?

58
00:06:50.453 --> 00:06:52.538
Aye, and fought valiantly.

59
00:06:52.622 --> 00:06:56.167
But last night he fell in battle
to Duke Henry's men.

60
00:06:57.001 --> 00:06:58.419
I'm sorry, Sheila.

61
00:06:59.712 --> 00:07:01.923
- Come on.
- You cretins!

62
00:07:02.798 --> 00:07:05.343
- Stop it, you bastards!
- Come on!

63
00:07:05.426 --> 00:07:07.261
You barbarian!

64
00:07:09.013 --> 00:07:13.351
Oh, no! Stop it! Stop it!
Get outta here, you little brats!

65
00:07:17.063 --> 00:07:18.773
Foul thing!

66
00:07:19.565 --> 00:07:22.360
A pox on you, brute!
Thou art a murderer!

67
00:07:22.443 --> 00:07:24.362
A black murderer!

68
00:07:29.450 --> 00:07:32.536
My brother's death
shall be avenged!

69
00:07:46.092 --> 00:07:48.511
Company, halt!

70
00:07:52.306 --> 00:07:54.558
Get that yoke off him!

71
00:07:56.185 --> 00:07:57.979
Kill them!

72
00:07:59.855 --> 00:08:01.065
Into the pit!

73
00:08:07.822 --> 00:08:11.450
You, sir,
are not one of my vassals.

74
00:08:12.493 --> 00:08:14.286
Who are you?

75
00:08:14.912 --> 00:08:16.497
Who wants to know?

76
00:08:17.581 --> 00:08:19.625
I am Henry the Red...

77
00:08:19.709 --> 00:08:24.171
Duke of Shael, Lord of the Northlands
and leader of its peoples.

78
00:08:25.006 --> 00:08:29.552
Well, hello, Mr. Fancy Pants.
I got news for you, pal.

79
00:08:29.635 --> 00:08:33.014
You ain't leadin' but two things right now:
Jack and shit.

80
00:08:33.097 --> 00:08:34.598
And Jack left town.

81
00:08:34.682 --> 00:08:39.228
- Shut your bleedin' hole!
- Gentlemen, Lord Arthur!

82
00:08:47.403 --> 00:08:50.990
There is an evil
awakened in this land.

83
00:08:51.073 --> 00:08:54.744
And while my people fight
for their very souls against it...

84
00:08:54.827 --> 00:08:57.747
you, Henry the Red,
wage war on us!

85
00:08:57.830 --> 00:08:59.832
Charlatan!

86
00:09:01.876 --> 00:09:04.837
It was you who first turned
your swords on us!

87
00:09:04.920 --> 00:09:07.965
And this evil has befouled
my people as well!

88
00:09:08.049 --> 00:09:11.135
Your people are no better
than the foul corruption...

89
00:09:11.218 --> 00:09:15.514
- that lies in the bowels of that pit.
- Right, you're no better.

90
00:09:15.598 --> 00:09:18.601
May God
have mercy upon your souls.

91
00:09:33.115 --> 00:09:37.369
May God
have mercy upon your souls.

92
00:09:41.874 --> 00:09:45.628
Into the pit with those
bloodthirsty sons of whores!

93
00:09:45.711 --> 00:09:47.088
No!

94
00:09:47.838 --> 00:09:49.215
No!

95
00:09:50.091 --> 00:09:51.884
No! No!

96
00:10:21.122 --> 00:10:23.499
Heavenly God!

97
00:10:26.460 --> 00:10:28.504
He's escaping!

98
00:10:28.587 --> 00:10:30.756
Hold him!

99
00:11:00.786 --> 00:11:03.122
- Who's next?
- It's him.

100
00:11:03.205 --> 00:11:04.832
He trembles!

101
00:11:05.416 --> 00:11:09.753
- They don't look so clever now, do they?
- He's frightened!

102
00:11:09.837 --> 00:11:12.256
He's frightened white!

103
00:11:15.009 --> 00:11:16.552
Wait a minute.

104
00:11:17.094 --> 00:11:22.141
Wait a minute.
You gotta understand, man.

105
00:11:22.224 --> 00:11:26.020
I never even saw
these assholes before.

106
00:11:26.103 --> 00:11:29.190
- He trembles!
- He's begging!

107
00:11:29.273 --> 00:11:31.358
What are you waitin' for?

108
00:11:31.442 --> 00:11:34.403
Henry, you gotta tell him
you don't know me.

109
00:11:34.486 --> 00:11:36.530
We never met.
Tell him.

110
00:11:39.158 --> 00:11:41.869
I do not think
he'll listen, lad.

111
00:11:43.329 --> 00:11:47.625
Look...
I'm tellin' you, you got the wrong guy.

112
00:11:57.676 --> 00:12:01.889
I'm tellin' you,
you got the wrong guy.

113
00:12:56.902 --> 00:12:59.780
How do you like the pit?
Isn't the pit wonderful?

114
00:13:17.131 --> 00:13:18.757
Why, you...

115
00:13:23.554 --> 00:13:25.347
Spikes.

116
00:13:25.431 --> 00:13:29.143
Hey, he says, "spikes".
Give him spikes!

117
00:13:42.531 --> 00:13:44.450
Make way!

118
00:13:44.533 --> 00:13:46.368
Strange one!

119
00:13:57.212 --> 00:13:58.088
Strange one!

120
00:14:05.179 --> 00:14:06.096
Yes!

121
00:14:23.572 --> 00:14:26.075
Damn you.
Damn you!

122
00:15:50.659 --> 00:15:53.078
You know,
your shoelace is untied.

123
00:16:04.131 --> 00:16:05.841
Alright.

124
00:16:07.301 --> 00:16:09.720
Who wants some?

125
00:16:09.803 --> 00:16:11.805
Who's next?

126
00:16:11.889 --> 00:16:14.766
Huh...?
How 'bout it?

127
00:16:15.684 --> 00:16:18.020
Who wants some? Huh?

128
00:16:18.103 --> 00:16:20.522
Who wants to have a little?

129
00:16:24.902 --> 00:16:26.570
You.

130
00:16:28.906 --> 00:16:31.492
You want some more?

131
00:16:36.038 --> 00:16:38.165
You want a little?

132
00:16:40.042 --> 00:16:41.835
DO ya?

133
00:16:41.919 --> 00:16:44.630
Do ya want some more?
Huh?

134
00:16:59.436 --> 00:17:03.357
Now get on those horses
and get outta here.

135
00:17:06.109 --> 00:17:08.111
Let 'em go!

136
00:17:30.425 --> 00:17:31.927
Halt!

137
00:17:33.428 --> 00:17:36.723
Thank you, generous hosts!

138
00:17:36.807 --> 00:17:38.809
Sword boy!

139
00:17:46.525 --> 00:17:50.988
For that arrogance,
I shall see you dead.

140
00:18:00.914 --> 00:18:02.541
Yeah...

141
00:18:03.083 --> 00:18:07.004
Alright, you primitive screwheads,
listen up.

142
00:18:07.087 --> 00:18:08.964
See this?

143
00:18:09.464 --> 00:18:13.677
This... is my boom stick!

144
00:18:14.428 --> 00:18:18.890
It's a 12-gauge, double-barreled Remington.
S-mart's top of the line.

145
00:18:18.974 --> 00:18:22.019
You can find this
in the sporting goods department.

146
00:18:22.686 --> 00:18:25.522
That's right. This sweet baby
was made in Grand Rapids, Michigan.

147
00:18:26.189 --> 00:18:29.026
Retails for about $109.95.

148
00:18:29.109 --> 00:18:34.448
It's got a walnut stock,
cobalt blue steel and a hair trigger.

149
00:18:34.531 --> 00:18:39.953
That's right.
Shop smart, shop S-mart.

150
00:18:40.037 --> 00:18:42.539
- You got that?
- Yes, sir. Right.

151
00:18:42.623 --> 00:18:44.916
Now I swear...

152
00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:48.253
the next one of you primates...

153
00:18:48.337 --> 00:18:51.173
even touches me...

154
00:19:20.077 --> 00:19:24.706
Now, let's talk about
how I get back home.

155
00:19:55.737 --> 00:19:58.407
I prithee to forgive me,
my Lord.

156
00:19:58.490 --> 00:20:01.201
I believed thee
one of Henry's men.

157
00:20:01.284 --> 00:20:04.621
First you wanna kill me,
now you wanna kiss me...

158
00:20:06.039 --> 00:20:07.874
Blow.

159
00:20:11.211 --> 00:20:14.131
So what's the deal?
Can you send me back or not?

160
00:20:14.214 --> 00:20:16.425
Only the Necronomicon
has the power.

161
00:20:16.508 --> 00:20:18.760
An unholy book
which we also require.

162
00:20:18.844 --> 00:20:22.973
Within its pages are passages
that can send you back to your time.

163
00:20:23.056 --> 00:20:26.893
Only you, The Promised One,
can quest for it.

164
00:20:26.977 --> 00:20:29.938
I don't want your book.
I don't want your bullshit.

165
00:20:30.021 --> 00:20:33.817
Just send me back to my own time.
Pronto, today, chop...

166
00:20:43.410 --> 00:20:46.371
You shall die!

167
00:20:52.002 --> 00:20:55.839
You shall never obtain
the Necronomicon!

168
00:20:55.922 --> 00:21:00.802
We shall feast upon your souls!

169
00:21:23.074 --> 00:21:25.952
It's a trick.
Get an axe.

170
00:21:32.501 --> 00:21:36.213
Guards, stop it!
Catch the witch!

171
00:21:36.296 --> 00:21:39.007
- Death to the witch! Death to...!
- Have some porridge!

172
00:21:39.090 --> 00:21:43.053
My eyes! I'm blind!
Oh, God, I'm blind!

173
00:21:51.019 --> 00:21:53.188
Yo, she-bitch.

174
00:21:54.272 --> 00:21:56.149
Let's go.

175
00:22:18.171 --> 00:22:20.507
If the Necronomicon fell into
the hands of the Deadites...

176
00:22:20.590 --> 00:22:23.635
all mankind will be consumed
by this evil.

177
00:22:23.718 --> 00:22:26.763
Now will thou
quest for the book?

178
00:22:39.609 --> 00:22:41.236
That one.

179
00:23:08.513 --> 00:23:10.390
Groovy.

180
00:23:23.194 --> 00:23:26.364
What's the matter? You raised in a barn?
Shut the door.

181
00:23:26.448 --> 00:23:29.993
Probably was raised in a barn,
with all the other primitives.

182
00:23:38.919 --> 00:23:42.005
The wise men say that
thou art The Promised One.

183
00:23:45.800 --> 00:23:49.054
'Tis said that thou wilt journey
for the book to help us...

184
00:23:49.137 --> 00:23:51.473
and that thou wilt lead
our people against the evil.

185
00:23:51.556 --> 00:23:55.518
The only reason I'm going
to get the book is to get home.

186
00:24:01.316 --> 00:24:04.945
- I believe thou wilt be leaving in the morning.
- Don't touch that, please!

187
00:24:05.028 --> 00:24:08.823
Your primitive intellect wouldn't understand
alloys and compositions...

188
00:24:08.907 --> 00:24:11.451
and things with
molecular structures in the...

189
00:24:14.704 --> 00:24:16.748
What are you doin' here anyway?

190
00:24:17.624 --> 00:24:22.003
I wanted to say that all of my hopes
and prayers go with you.

191
00:24:22.087 --> 00:24:24.631
And I made this for thee.

192
00:24:25.298 --> 00:24:28.218
Good, I could use
a horse blanket.

193
00:24:50.198 --> 00:24:52.492
Gimme some sugar, baby.

194
00:25:57.265 --> 00:25:59.100
Come on, boy!

195
00:26:20.288 --> 00:26:21.790
Steady now. Whoa.

196
00:26:27.462 --> 00:26:29.130
What? What is it?

197
00:26:29.214 --> 00:26:33.885
This path will lead you
to an unholy place, a cemetery.

198
00:26:33.968 --> 00:26:37.013
There, the Necronomicon awaits.

199
00:26:39.891 --> 00:26:43.478
When thou retrievest the book from
its cradle, you must recite the words:

200
00:26:43.561 --> 00:26:46.815
Klaatu barada nikto.

201
00:26:46.898 --> 00:26:50.401
Klaatu... barada... nikto.
Okay.

202
00:26:50.485 --> 00:26:52.570
Well, repeat them.

203
00:26:52.654 --> 00:26:55.198
Klaatu barada nikto.

204
00:26:55.281 --> 00:26:57.659
- Again!
- I got it, I got it!

205
00:26:57.742 --> 00:27:02.205
I know your damn words, alright?
Now you get this straight, the both of you.

206
00:27:02.288 --> 00:27:05.291
If I get that book,
you send me back.

207
00:27:05.375 --> 00:27:07.752
After that, I'm history.

208
00:28:11.316 --> 00:28:13.234
What is it, boy?

209
00:28:36.716 --> 00:28:38.384
Come on!

210
00:28:50.939 --> 00:28:52.398
Come on!

211
00:29:07.538 --> 00:29:08.998
Come on, you!

212
00:32:25.862 --> 00:32:28.322
Ramming speed!

213
00:32:35.913 --> 00:32:37.665
- Ready.
- Aim.

214
00:32:37.748 --> 00:32:38.875
Fire!

215
00:32:43.921 --> 00:32:47.425
Yeah, Baby!
Yeah, Baby!

216
00:32:49.677 --> 00:32:51.554
- Hey, don't point that thing my way!
- Me either!

217
00:32:51.637 --> 00:32:53.556
- Look out!
- Game change, boys!

218
00:32:53.639 --> 00:32:55.600
Shake a leg!

219
00:33:01.606 --> 00:33:03.274
You lousy little...

220
00:33:06.611 --> 00:33:08.321
Oh, hold on!

221
00:33:11.949 --> 00:33:15.536
Yeah!
I'm gonna hunt down all you...

222
00:33:32.178 --> 00:33:33.971
You little bastards!

223
00:33:34.055 --> 00:33:36.682
Alright, I'll crush
each and every one of you.

224
00:33:36.766 --> 00:33:38.768
I'll crush you to pieces,
I'm telling you!

225
00:33:38.851 --> 00:33:42.146
I'll squash you so hard,
you'll have to look up to see...

226
00:33:42.230 --> 00:33:43.564
Hey, dumb ass!

227
00:33:47.652 --> 00:33:49.278
Surf's up!

228
00:34:00.122 --> 00:34:01.916
All together now!

229
00:34:19.267 --> 00:34:20.977
Oh shit!

230
00:34:28.442 --> 00:34:30.152
Oops.

231
00:34:31.612 --> 00:34:33.990
Quietly... gently...

232
00:34:41.539 --> 00:34:42.790
Easy, big fella! Easy!

233
00:34:57.305 --> 00:35:00.433
<i>London Bridge is falling down</i>

234
00:35:00.516 --> 00:35:02.810
Falling down

235
00:35:03.311 --> 00:35:05.896
Falling down!

236
00:35:07.481 --> 00:35:09.442
<i>M y fair lady!</i>

237
00:35:21.078 --> 00:35:23.664
Hey, is he up?
How is he?

238
00:35:23.748 --> 00:35:25.666
Hey, he got up...

239
00:35:31.339 --> 00:35:34.050
What a horrible nightmare...

240
00:35:35.676 --> 00:35:37.094
Wait a minute...

241
00:35:37.178 --> 00:35:39.305
Oh, God!

242
00:35:40.097 --> 00:35:42.725
I can't move!

243
00:35:52.026 --> 00:35:54.195
You got me?

244
00:35:54.278 --> 00:35:56.322
Open wide!

245
00:35:57.156 --> 00:35:58.574
Let's go!

246
00:35:59.992 --> 00:36:02.370
Geronimo!

247
00:36:05.748 --> 00:36:07.625
- Hooray!
- Hooray!

248
00:36:08.834 --> 00:36:10.711
Let's go!

249
00:36:33.651 --> 00:36:36.112
Okay, little fella.

250
00:36:36.195 --> 00:36:39.156
How about
some hot chocolate, huh?

251
00:36:48.582 --> 00:36:52.753
How'd you like the taste of that, huh?
How'd you like the taste...?

252
00:37:10.771 --> 00:37:14.191
Oh, clear God,
it's growing bigger!

253
00:37:36.046 --> 00:37:39.675
- Hey! What's the big idea takin'...?
- Hey! What's the big idea takin'...?

254
00:37:39.759 --> 00:37:41.761
- Why, you...
- Why, you...

255
00:37:45.264 --> 00:37:48.309
Oh, I'm blind!
I'm blind!

256
00:37:58.444 --> 00:38:00.821
Where are you takin' me?

257
00:38:00.905 --> 00:38:04.742
Oh, Susanna,
don't you cry for me!

258
00:38:04.825 --> 00:38:09.246
I've come from Alabama
with a banjo on my knee.

259
00:38:22.593 --> 00:38:24.512
What are you?

260
00:38:24.595 --> 00:38:26.180
Are you me?

261
00:38:26.263 --> 00:38:28.808
"What are you?
Are you me?"

262
00:38:30.309 --> 00:38:32.061
You sound like a jerk!

263
00:38:32.144 --> 00:38:34.396
- Why are you doing this?
- Oh, you wanna know?

264
00:38:34.480 --> 00:38:36.690
'Cause the answer's easy:

265
00:38:36.774 --> 00:38:40.444
I'm bad Ash,
and you're good Ash.

266
00:38:40.528 --> 00:38:42.404
You're goody
little two-shoes.

267
00:38:42.488 --> 00:38:46.200
You're goody little two-shoes,
goody little two-shoes.

268
00:38:46.742 --> 00:38:49.453
Little goody two-shoes.
Little goody two-shoes.

269
00:38:49.537 --> 00:38:51.997
Little goody two-shoes.
Little goody two-shoes!

270
00:38:52.081 --> 00:38:55.417
Little goody two-shoes!
Little goody two-shoes!

271
00:38:59.672 --> 00:39:01.590
Little goody two-shoes!

272
00:39:13.644 --> 00:39:15.896
I ain't that good.

273
00:40:28.928 --> 00:40:31.263
Now you see what's what.

274
00:40:32.306 --> 00:40:36.060
A man's body is his own
personal property.

275
00:40:36.727 --> 00:40:39.730
Don't let anybody try
and take that away from me.

276
00:40:41.649 --> 00:40:45.861
That'll teach you.
Yeah, that'll teach you.

277
00:40:47.988 --> 00:40:50.574
You shall never retrieve
the Necronomicon!

278
00:40:50.658 --> 00:40:53.869
You'll die in the graveyard
before you get it!

279
00:40:53.953 --> 00:40:57.706
Hey... What's that
you got on your face?

280
00:40:59.875 --> 00:41:03.837
- See how that works?
- I'll come back for you!

281
00:41:03.921 --> 00:41:05.214
I...

282
00:41:22.648 --> 00:41:24.608
Come on, boy!

283
00:41:39.039 --> 00:41:40.499
Come on!

284
00:42:58.577 --> 00:42:59.787
Three books?

285
00:43:04.333 --> 00:43:06.752
Wait a minute.
Hold it.

286
00:43:06.835 --> 00:43:10.380
Nobody said anything
about three books.

287
00:43:11.006 --> 00:43:13.926
Oh, that stinkin' wise man!
He was so busy...

288
00:43:14.009 --> 00:43:17.262
filling me full of his secret little words,
his phrases and his bullshit...

289
00:43:17.346 --> 00:43:20.307
that he never said
anything about this!

290
00:43:20.849 --> 00:43:25.854
What am I supposed to do?
Take one book, or all books, or...

291
00:43:25.938 --> 00:43:27.940
or what?

292
00:43:30.484 --> 00:43:32.236
Well...

293
00:44:30.711 --> 00:44:33.630
Whoa... Wrong book.

294
00:45:37.027 --> 00:45:38.820
Oh, you...

295
00:45:38.904 --> 00:45:41.198
I'll get back to you.

296
00:45:42.699 --> 00:45:44.409
Well...

297
00:45:45.744 --> 00:45:48.413
Seems fairly obvious.

298
00:45:51.750 --> 00:45:53.752
Oh! Wait a minute.

299
00:45:53.835 --> 00:45:56.338
The words.
Alright, alright, alright.

300
00:45:56.421 --> 00:45:58.757
Say the words...

301
00:46:01.969 --> 00:46:03.470
Klaatu...

302
00:46:03.553 --> 00:46:05.222
barada...

303
00:46:05.305 --> 00:46:06.848
... n...

304
00:46:13.730 --> 00:46:15.274
Necktie.

305
00:46:15.357 --> 00:46:16.817
Nectar.

306
00:46:16.900 --> 00:46:18.610
Nickel.

307
00:46:18.694 --> 00:46:20.279
Noodle.

308
00:46:20.362 --> 00:46:24.074
It's an "N" word.
It's definitely an "N" word.

309
00:46:26.285 --> 00:46:28.912
It's definitely an "N" word.

310
00:46:40.340 --> 00:46:43.593
Klaatu... barada...

311
00:46:43.677 --> 00:46:45.595
... n...

312
00:46:58.984 --> 00:47:00.819
Okay, then!

313
00:47:01.737 --> 00:47:03.780
That's it.

314
00:47:13.582 --> 00:47:14.958
Hey!

315
00:47:15.500 --> 00:47:18.503
Wait a minute!
Everything's cool!

316
00:47:18.587 --> 00:47:21.590
I said the words.
I did!

317
00:47:22.716 --> 00:47:24.885
No, wait!

318
00:47:38.815 --> 00:47:42.611
You people, seek cover!
To the parapet!

319
00:47:43.278 --> 00:47:45.822
Seek your children!

320
00:47:46.948 --> 00:47:49.076
Steady the horses!

321
00:47:49.159 --> 00:47:52.245
Something's wrong.
Something's amiss.

322
00:48:24.653 --> 00:48:26.988
Where'd you go?
Where'd you...

323
00:49:02.649 --> 00:49:05.402
I'll crush ya!
I'll mash ya into paste, you bony crea...

324
00:49:14.828 --> 00:49:18.623
Keep your damn filthy bones
out of my mouth.

325
00:49:43.273 --> 00:49:45.609
I'm through
being their garbage boy.

326
00:49:45.692 --> 00:49:48.445
I did my part.
Now I want back...

327
00:49:48.528 --> 00:49:50.780
like in the deal!

328
00:50:04.503 --> 00:50:08.173
I... live...

329
00:50:09.799 --> 00:50:12.177
again.

330
00:50:21.728 --> 00:50:25.690
There! The Promised One!
The Promised One's returned!

331
00:50:25.774 --> 00:50:28.401
Raise the portcullis!

332
00:50:33.949 --> 00:50:36.952
Welcome home!

333
00:50:37.035 --> 00:50:39.663
We're saved!

334
00:50:39.746 --> 00:50:43.875
- The Necronomicon!
- Truly he is The Promised One!

335
00:50:43.959 --> 00:50:46.127
- He's brought the Necronomicon!
- How are ya?

336
00:50:46.211 --> 00:50:48.463
- He's brought the book!
- Yeah, great, great.

337
00:50:48.547 --> 00:50:52.133
- Good boy!
- Get the fuck outta my face!

338
00:50:58.098 --> 00:51:02.394
The Necronomicon, quickly.
Did you bring the Necronomicon?

339
00:51:03.061 --> 00:51:05.689
- Yeah, it's, it's just that...
- Just what?

340
00:51:07.148 --> 00:51:09.484
Nothin'. Here.

341
00:51:16.074 --> 00:51:18.994
Now send me back.
Like in the deal.

342
00:51:19.077 --> 00:51:21.329
When you removed the Necronomicon
from the cradle...

343
00:51:21.413 --> 00:51:23.915
did you speak the words?

344
00:51:23.999 --> 00:51:27.043
- Yeah, basically.
- Did you speak the exact words?

345
00:51:27.127 --> 00:51:30.088
Look, maybe I didn't say
every single, little tiny syllable, no...

346
00:51:30.171 --> 00:51:32.841
- ... but basically I said 'em, yeah.
- Dung-eating fool!

347
00:51:32.924 --> 00:51:35.010
Thou hast doomed us all!

348
00:51:35.093 --> 00:51:38.763
When thou misspoke the words,
the army of the dead awoke!

349
00:51:38.847 --> 00:51:41.057
W, whoa, whoa,
right there, spinach chin.

350
00:51:41.141 --> 00:51:44.185
You said you could clean this mess up
once you got that book.

351
00:51:44.269 --> 00:51:48.189
You said there was a passage that
could get rid of this thing and send me back.

352
00:51:48.273 --> 00:51:50.833
It's true, the book still possesses
the power to send you back...

353
00:51:50.900 --> 00:51:52.736
but to us it is useless!

354
00:51:52.819 --> 00:51:55.447
The evil has a terrible hunger
for the Necronomicon...

355
00:51:55.530 --> 00:51:58.408
and it will come here
to get it.

356
00:51:58.491 --> 00:52:01.161
We had a deal.

357
00:52:01.244 --> 00:52:04.080
You wanted the damn book,
I got it for ya.

358
00:52:04.164 --> 00:52:06.207
I did my part,
now you send me back.

359
00:52:06.291 --> 00:52:13.006
Very well. As we are men of our word,
we shall honor our bargain.

360
00:52:13.089 --> 00:52:16.176
The wise men shall return you
to your own time.

361
00:52:17.093 --> 00:52:19.095
Yeah?

362
00:52:19.179 --> 00:52:23.391
- I thought he was the one.
- Yeah, right, 'cause that was the deal.

363
00:52:23.475 --> 00:52:28.396
So when do you think we can start
with all the...

364
00:52:28.480 --> 00:52:32.025
- ... thing and the...
- He's nothin' but a traitor, he is!

365
00:52:32.108 --> 00:52:36.780
When do you think we can start...
with all the ceremony and...

366
00:52:36.863 --> 00:52:38.657
You know, like...

367
00:52:38.740 --> 00:52:43.119
You know, 'cause...
sooner is always better than later, right?

368
00:52:44.120 --> 00:52:46.665
Wretched excuse for a man!

369
00:52:46.748 --> 00:52:49.793
The wise men were fools
to trust in you.

370
00:52:50.877 --> 00:52:55.757
- I knew he couldn't be trusted.
- We put our trust in him.

371
00:52:55.840 --> 00:52:58.843
I still believe
that thou wilt help us.

372
00:52:58.927 --> 00:53:02.722
Oh, Sheila, don't you get it?
It's over.

373
00:53:04.224 --> 00:53:06.685
I didn't have what it took.

374
00:53:08.645 --> 00:53:10.563
So long.

375
00:53:15.110 --> 00:53:17.195
You would leave me?

376
00:53:17.278 --> 00:53:20.365
Cripes, I don't belong here.

377
00:53:21.491 --> 00:53:23.576
I got a chance to go back,
and I'm takin' it.

378
00:53:23.660 --> 00:53:26.037
But what of the things
we've shared?

379
00:53:26.121 --> 00:53:28.790
What of all the sweet words
that you spoke in private?

380
00:53:28.873 --> 00:53:30.750
Aw, well...

381
00:53:31.668 --> 00:53:35.839
Well, that's just what we call pillow talk, baby.
That's all.

382
00:53:35.922 --> 00:53:38.383
It was more than that.

383
00:53:39.759 --> 00:53:42.387
I still have faith in thee.

384
00:53:42.470 --> 00:53:45.974
I still believe that thou
wilt stay and save us.

385
00:53:51.438 --> 00:53:53.314
Coward!

386
00:53:56.818 --> 00:53:58.987
Look there! A demon!

387
00:53:59.946 --> 00:54:02.782
Draw, lads,
for Lord and castle!

388
00:54:11.374 --> 00:54:13.168
Let's get out of here!

389
00:54:14.794 --> 00:54:17.630
Ash, help me!

390
00:54:17.714 --> 00:54:19.048
Sheila!

391
00:54:32.687 --> 00:54:35.565
Hold your arms!
You'll hit the girl!

392
00:54:39.944 --> 00:54:41.988
Me sword!

393
00:54:46.576 --> 00:54:49.037
Damn you!

394
00:55:06.304 --> 00:55:09.307
Dig, damn you!

395
00:55:09.390 --> 00:55:11.434
Dig faster!

396
00:55:11.518 --> 00:55:16.064
I shall command every worm-infested
son-of-a-bitch that ever died in battle!

397
00:55:16.147 --> 00:55:18.483
- You there, handsomely now.
- Aye, my liege.

398
00:55:18.566 --> 00:55:21.277
We shall storm their castle
and get my book.

399
00:55:21.361 --> 00:55:24.531
Hoist, you damnable varlets!

400
00:55:28.368 --> 00:55:32.622
Welcome back
to the land of the living.

401
00:55:32.705 --> 00:55:35.875
Now pick up a shovel
and get digging!

402
00:55:37.418 --> 00:55:39.629
Bring on the Wench!

403
00:55:51.099 --> 00:55:53.184
Gimme some sugar, baby.

404
00:55:59.065 --> 00:56:03.736
Now, ain't you
a sweet little thing?

405
00:56:06.656 --> 00:56:09.701
Don't touch me, you foul thing!

406
00:56:21.254 --> 00:56:23.423
Come on.

407
00:56:23.506 --> 00:56:25.884
That's it.

408
00:56:38.688 --> 00:56:42.150
We got plans for you, girly-girl.
Move!

409
00:56:43.443 --> 00:56:48.406
Have you lost your bones,
you decomposed gobs? Get thee hence!

410
00:56:56.623 --> 00:56:59.250
A scout approaches!

411
00:57:05.298 --> 00:57:07.634
Hey, get his horse.

412
00:57:08.259 --> 00:57:09.344
Arise.

413
00:57:09.427 --> 00:57:13.139
An army of the dead gather in the wilderness.
They approach the castle.

414
00:57:13.222 --> 00:57:15.767
- How far from here?
- But two days' ride.

415
00:57:15.850 --> 00:57:17.685
These winged ones
are only the first of them.

416
00:57:17.769 --> 00:57:20.521
- Perhaps we should leave as soon as possible.
- We could be safe in the mountains.

417
00:57:20.605 --> 00:57:22.315
Yes, yes, the mountains!
We must flee!

418
00:57:22.398 --> 00:57:25.109
- It is written, Arthur. It has been foretold.
- They'll take our souls.

419
00:57:25.193 --> 00:57:28.488
- I'm afraid! I don't want to die!
- They'll swallow our souls.

420
00:57:30.198 --> 00:57:32.116
That's it.

421
00:57:32.784 --> 00:57:34.702
Go ahead and run.

422
00:57:34.786 --> 00:57:38.081
Run home and cry to mama!

423
00:57:38.164 --> 00:57:40.208
Me?

424
00:57:40.291 --> 00:57:42.919
I'm through runnin'!

425
00:57:43.753 --> 00:57:47.048
I say we stay here
and fight it out.

426
00:57:47.131 --> 00:57:51.678
Are all men from
the future loudmouthed braggarts?

427
00:57:51.761 --> 00:57:53.429
Nope.

428
00:57:53.513 --> 00:57:56.724
Just me, baby.
Just me.

429
00:57:57.350 --> 00:58:01.312
How will we fight an army of the dead
at our castle walls?

430
00:58:01.396 --> 00:58:04.232
How will you fight that?
More words?

431
00:58:04.315 --> 00:58:08.987
Most of our people have already fled.
We are but 60 men.

432
00:58:09.070 --> 00:58:12.490
Then we'll get Henry the Red
and his men to fight with us.

433
00:58:15.827 --> 00:58:19.914
Now... who's with me?

434
00:58:34.053 --> 00:58:36.472
I'll stand by ya.

435
00:58:38.099 --> 00:58:40.601
You can count on my steel.

436
00:58:40.685 --> 00:58:44.647
- I'll offer up my courage.
- Me sword's by his side.

437
00:58:44.731 --> 00:58:48.276
- I'm with you!
- I'll bend my bow to your will, sir.

438
00:58:48.359 --> 00:58:50.069
And mine!

439
00:58:51.696 --> 00:58:55.199
- We'll stand by you!
- Hail! Hail!

440
00:58:55.283 --> 00:58:57.577
Hail! Hail!

441
00:58:57.660 --> 00:59:00.204
Hail! Hail!

442
00:59:00.288 --> 00:59:03.207
Hail! Hail!

443
00:59:13.092 --> 00:59:17.805
Well, my clear,
say hello to the boys.

444
00:59:22.977 --> 00:59:26.898
There's a sight for sore bones.

445
00:59:30.526 --> 00:59:36.449
I may be bad,
but I feel... good.

446
00:59:36.532 --> 00:59:39.285
- Who rules?
- You, my Lord!

447
00:59:39.368 --> 00:59:42.872
- You, sir! To the castle!
- To the castle!

448
00:59:42.955 --> 00:59:46.501
- But the men are afraid!
- Has Duke Henry not answered us yet?

449
00:59:46.584 --> 00:59:49.128
Quit your belly-aching!

450
00:59:49.212 --> 00:59:51.506
I know you're scared.

451
00:59:52.256 --> 00:59:54.342
We're all scared.

452
00:59:54.926 --> 00:59:57.970
But that doesn't mean
we're cowards.

453
00:59:58.054 --> 01:00:01.182
We can take these Deadites,
we can take 'em!

454
01:00:02.517 --> 01:00:04.519
With science.

455
01:00:08.189 --> 01:00:13.444
- Come to it! Come!
- Come on, fellas! Push!

456
01:01:04.036 --> 01:01:07.290
Come on! Come on!
Tilt! Tilt! Tilt!

457
01:01:07.957 --> 01:01:09.292
Okay, in, in!

458
01:01:51.626 --> 01:01:53.294
Yeah!

459
01:01:55.046 --> 01:01:59.175
They're coming!
The Deadites approach!

460
01:02:04.222 --> 01:02:07.725
Quickly now, you worthless fools!
They'll be on us anon!

461
01:02:07.808 --> 01:02:11.896
- Come on, guys!
- Archers to the back!

462
01:02:13.522 --> 01:02:17.860
The moment of truth is almost here.
You men better not fail me now.

463
01:02:34.001 --> 01:02:36.504
There's so damned many of them.

464
01:02:49.809 --> 01:02:52.061
I need more men.

465
01:03:34.228 --> 01:03:38.649
Battle stations!
Get those rocks up, mister, on the double!

466
01:03:38.733 --> 01:03:43.279
Ready the catapults!
By God, let's give 'em what for.

467
01:03:49.118 --> 01:03:50.995
Keep it together!

468
01:03:51.078 --> 01:03:55.374
- And halt!
- Company, halt!

469
01:03:55.458 --> 01:03:57.585
Company, halt!

470
01:04:58.270 --> 01:05:01.399
- Looking glass!
- Aye, sire.

471
01:05:08.823 --> 01:05:11.784
Once I possess
the Necronomicon...

472
01:05:11.867 --> 01:05:17.832
I shall rule,
and you shall be my queen.

473
01:05:31.846 --> 01:05:34.723
My Lord, we are positioned
on both fronts.

474
01:05:34.807 --> 01:05:38.269
Fine, fine, fine.
Where are they keeping my book?

475
01:05:38.352 --> 01:05:41.272
There, my Lord,
beyond the drawbridge in the second wall.

476
01:05:41.355 --> 01:05:43.566
That would be the safest place.

477
01:05:43.649 --> 01:05:49.071
I will not allow anything to keep me
from possessing that Necronomicon.

478
01:05:50.114 --> 01:05:54.660
Now, bring me forth
into that castle.

479
01:05:54.743 --> 01:05:57.830
- Forward!
- Forward!

480
01:05:57.913 --> 01:06:02.334
Cry havoc,
and let loose the clogs of war!

481
01:06:02.418 --> 01:06:05.212
To the castle!

482
01:06:09.508 --> 01:06:10.885
Excellent.

483
01:06:13.721 --> 01:06:16.348
Death to the mortals!

484
01:06:19.560 --> 01:06:20.686
Arrows!

485
01:06:21.270 --> 01:06:22.980
Bows!

486
01:06:23.063 --> 01:06:24.899
Load!

487
01:06:25.900 --> 01:06:27.776
Draw!

488
01:06:37.119 --> 01:06:39.538
Torch boy!

489
01:07:21.372 --> 01:07:22.623
Steady.

490
01:07:29.421 --> 01:07:30.756
Fire!

491
01:07:33.300 --> 01:07:35.928
Advance, you demons!
Advance

492
01:07:57.324 --> 01:07:59.952
Yeah, baby!

493
01:08:07.543 --> 01:08:09.128
Alright!

494
01:08:09.211 --> 01:08:12.965
- Retreat! Retreat!
- Let's get the hell out of here!

495
01:08:21.932 --> 01:08:24.018
Damn him!

496
01:08:25.102 --> 01:08:27.938
The sortie on the second flank
will stand.

497
01:08:28.022 --> 01:08:29.857
It must.

498
01:08:30.566 --> 01:08:33.986
Sire, there's a second division
approaching from the south.

499
01:08:34.945 --> 01:08:37.906
Ram the gates!

500
01:08:42.286 --> 01:08:43.787
Catapults.

501
01:08:43.871 --> 01:08:46.165
Catapults! South!

502
01:08:46.248 --> 01:08:49.585
Come on, men! Move it!
Turn it around!

503
01:08:49.668 --> 01:08:51.754
Right! Heave-ho!

504
01:08:52.796 --> 01:08:57.384
- We'll crush them!
- We'll strike again!

505
01:09:06.852 --> 01:09:07.561
Yeah!

506
01:09:09.313 --> 01:09:11.273
Fire!

507
01:09:16.820 --> 01:09:19.740
- Look there!
- What the blazes?

508
01:09:27.247 --> 01:09:29.833
- Watch out!
- Make way!

509
01:09:33.170 --> 01:09:34.088
Yeah!

510
01:09:36.298 --> 01:09:37.633
Seek cover!

511
01:09:47.518 --> 01:09:50.479
Oh, you miserable
bags of bones!

512
01:09:50.562 --> 01:09:54.316
Pick yourselves up
and sally for...

513
01:09:55.192 --> 01:09:56.860
Sally f...

514
01:09:57.778 --> 01:09:59.655
Sally forth!

515
01:10:03.575 --> 01:10:05.953
Come on,
you miserable hotheads!

516
01:10:07.079 --> 01:10:08.664
Lower!

517
01:10:08.747 --> 01:10:10.416
Heave!

518
01:10:16.547 --> 01:10:18.215
Forward!

519
01:10:20.426 --> 01:10:23.220
Buttress the door, now!

520
01:10:35.190 --> 01:10:36.275
Hold fast!

521
01:10:39.611 --> 01:10:42.281
- Rocks!
- Stone these creatures!

522
01:10:42.364 --> 01:10:44.116
Damn you!

523
01:10:47.119 --> 01:10:49.246
Ooh, that's gotta hurt.

524
01:10:49.329 --> 01:10:52.166
Go, you cretins!
Arrows!

525
01:10:52.249 --> 01:10:54.793
Load! Fire!

526
01:11:00.299 --> 01:11:02.551
We'll ram it down
the bastard's throat!

527
01:11:04.428 --> 01:11:05.846
Fire!

528
01:11:10.809 --> 01:11:14.062
South flank, to the western wall!
Now!

529
01:11:14.146 --> 01:11:17.733
Where is Henry the Red?
I told you he would not come!

530
01:11:17.816 --> 01:11:20.360
Keep your sardine can on,
bucket-head!

531
01:11:20.444 --> 01:11:22.946
I said he'll be here,
he'll be here!

532
01:11:23.030 --> 01:11:25.783
I think he will not.
But know this:

533
01:11:25.866 --> 01:11:28.076
No matter
how this battle fares...

534
01:11:28.160 --> 01:11:31.705
I was wrong to think
you a coward.

535
01:11:36.668 --> 01:11:39.087
We've broken through!
The castle is ours!

536
01:11:44.426 --> 01:11:47.554
Kill the mortals!

537
01:12:23.549 --> 01:12:26.927
They've breached the first wall!
What next?

538
01:12:33.809 --> 01:12:36.562
We are deserted!

539
01:12:37.396 --> 01:12:40.232
Fall back!
Man the parapet!

540
01:12:40.315 --> 01:12:42.526
Protect the book!

541
01:12:43.235 --> 01:12:45.195
God save us all.

542
01:12:45.279 --> 01:12:49.408
Up the ladders, lads!
To the safety of the parapets!

543
01:13:00.085 --> 01:13:03.255
Say hello to the 21st century.
Yeah!

544
01:13:15.934 --> 01:13:18.186
Come on!
I got plenty for everybody!

545
01:13:19.354 --> 01:13:20.272
Look out!

546
01:13:27.446 --> 01:13:29.615
- How do you like this?
- Play dead!

547
01:13:32.784 --> 01:13:36.371
It's the one in the cart we want.
Get him!

548
01:13:53.221 --> 01:13:55.432
Sayonara, sucker!

549
01:14:01.647 --> 01:14:03.315
Why, you...

550
01:14:04.983 --> 01:14:07.778
You can run,
but you can't hide!

551
01:14:33.595 --> 01:14:35.347
Sheila.

552
01:15:00.372 --> 01:15:03.709
- We've secured the courtyard, my lord.
- Excellent.

553
01:15:03.792 --> 01:15:06.962
Now I will have that book.
Storm the walls!

554
01:15:07.045 --> 01:15:10.215
- Ladders!
- Come on, you bony devils! Hurry up...

555
01:15:10.298 --> 01:15:13.677
or I'll send you to the glue factory!
Elmer!

556
01:15:14.177 --> 01:15:16.221
To the walls!

557
01:15:18.807 --> 01:15:22.519
I'll slice you to ribbons!
No, no! No, no! No! No!

558
01:15:46.293 --> 01:15:48.462
Hey! Look out!

559
01:15:55.302 --> 01:15:59.347
- Hey, you're mine, sweetie.
- Get off of her!

560
01:16:03.935 --> 01:16:05.645
Gotcha!

561
01:16:05.729 --> 01:16:07.647
Damn you!

562
01:16:07.731 --> 01:16:09.816
Defend the Necronomicon,
lads...

563
01:16:09.900 --> 01:16:12.944
or perish in the devil's fire!

564
01:16:16.823 --> 01:16:19.785
- My Lord!
- Stay with the book.

565
01:16:19.868 --> 01:16:22.329
The book's where we are.

566
01:16:40.847 --> 01:16:42.140
Oops!

567
01:16:44.184 --> 01:16:46.436
Hello friends!

568
01:16:54.945 --> 01:16:57.656
The book is mine!

569
01:17:11.586 --> 01:17:13.839
I'll cut your gizzard out.

570
01:17:14.464 --> 01:17:16.842
Hey! Where'd he go?
Hey!

571
01:17:27.352 --> 01:17:28.520
Come to papa!

572
01:17:30.188 --> 01:17:31.648
Get him!

573
01:18:00.844 --> 01:18:03.597
Crazy bitch, get off me!

574
01:18:03.680 --> 01:18:06.224
You're tearing my eyes out!

575
01:18:07.017 --> 01:18:08.560
You witch!

576
01:18:15.358 --> 01:18:17.068
Rig ht.

577
01:18:23.158 --> 01:18:26.077
You found me beautiful once.

578
01:18:26.161 --> 01:18:29.414
Honey, you got real ugly.

579
01:18:48.558 --> 01:18:50.060
There we are.

580
01:18:58.902 --> 01:19:02.447
So you wanna play rough, eh?
Okay

581
01:19:10.914 --> 01:19:13.208
Alright, alright.

582
01:19:36.648 --> 01:19:38.108
You're going down!

583
01:19:39.442 --> 01:19:42.946
- I'm goin' up.
- I'm comin' for ya.

584
01:19:55.875 --> 01:19:57.752
Come on!

585
01:20:13.393 --> 01:20:14.978
Get him!

586
01:20:15.979 --> 01:20:19.190
- Oops. Excuse me.
- Come on.

587
01:20:19.274 --> 01:20:20.900
Alright!

588
01:20:21.985 --> 01:20:26.323
You're pissin' me off,
you ugly son of a bitch!

589
01:20:47.844 --> 01:20:51.348
I'll spoil those good looks.

590
01:20:53.808 --> 01:20:55.852
Back-stabber!

591
01:21:01.066 --> 01:21:02.692
Hold still!

592
01:21:17.207 --> 01:21:18.708
Tally-hog

593
01:21:26.841 --> 01:21:29.761
- We can't hold the battlements!
- We will hold!

594
01:21:29.844 --> 01:21:31.721
We must protect the book!

595
01:21:31.805 --> 01:21:35.100
Where's Henry the Red?
Why's he not...?

596
01:21:36.101 --> 01:21:38.603
We are deserted!

597
01:21:39.938 --> 01:21:41.773
We're overwhelmed!

598
01:22:03.711 --> 01:22:06.714
I got a bone to pick with you.

599
01:22:06.798 --> 01:22:08.341
Come on!

600
01:22:14.431 --> 01:22:16.975
I'll slice your gizzard open!

601
01:22:34.242 --> 01:22:35.994
Now you're mine!

602
01:22:42.834 --> 01:22:44.294
No!

603
01:22:57.474 --> 01:22:59.184
Let go of the sword!

604
01:22:59.267 --> 01:23:03.563
I'll cut your throat out
if I get the chance.

605
01:23:25.293 --> 01:23:27.462
I have the book!

606
01:23:33.134 --> 01:23:35.428
I possess the Necronomicon!

607
01:23:35.512 --> 01:23:37.347
I've crushed
your pathetic army!

608
01:23:37.430 --> 01:23:39.182
Now I'll have my vengeance!

609
01:23:39.265 --> 01:23:43.144
The Red! The Red!
Duke Henry and his men have come!

610
01:23:43.228 --> 01:23:45.897
For king and castle!

611
01:23:45.980 --> 01:23:48.149
Cry havoc!

612
01:23:48.233 --> 01:23:53.238
Blows, blood, and death!

613
01:23:56.658 --> 01:23:58.451
We are saved!

614
01:24:09.295 --> 01:24:12.924
Onward, valiant cousins!
Their ranks are broke!

615
01:24:14.467 --> 01:24:16.844
Bloody hell!

616
01:24:16.928 --> 01:24:21.349
You've spoiled my plan for conquest,
and now you're going to die!

617
01:24:21.432 --> 01:24:25.228
Buckle up, bonehead,
'cause you're goin' for a ride.

618
01:24:40.535 --> 01:24:42.662
Victory's ours!

619
01:25:08.313 --> 01:25:11.733
- Tricky ones, they are.
- If it's a fight you want...

620
01:25:12.358 --> 01:25:15.236
Watch 'em, lads.
They're an untrustworthy lot.

621
01:25:15.320 --> 01:25:18.740
If it's a fight they're looking for,
they can get it!

622
01:26:08.748 --> 01:26:10.375
Move yourself, lad!

623
01:26:10.875 --> 01:26:12.877
- Your hand, man. Godspeed!
- Hey, Henry.

624
01:26:12.960 --> 01:26:14.379
- You had us going.
- My Lady.

625
01:26:14.462 --> 01:26:16.923
- Arthur.
- Well won, my friend.

626
01:26:17.006 --> 01:26:19.467
We've won the clay.
Yeah!

627
01:26:19.550 --> 01:26:21.594
Yeah!

628
01:26:25.098 --> 01:26:29.435
We're brothers!
And a new kingdom shall be born!

629
01:26:32.146 --> 01:26:37.110
The book tells us that each drop
allows a man to sleep for a century.

630
01:26:37.193 --> 01:26:42.448
Swallow six drops,
thou shall awaken in thine own time.

631
01:27:31.497 --> 01:27:33.291
Hyah, boy!

632
01:27:45.636 --> 01:27:48.014
God bless you, sire.

633
01:28:28.971 --> 01:28:30.807
Six drops.

634
01:28:33.643 --> 01:28:36.020
One, two, three...

635
01:28:36.687 --> 01:28:38.272
four...

636
01:28:39.106 --> 01:28:40.608
five..

637
01:28:48.199 --> 01:28:49.784
Five...

638
01:28:51.077 --> 01:28:52.662
six.

639
01:30:10.072 --> 01:30:12.283
I'm home

640
01:30:28.507 --> 01:30:30.092
Plastics!

641
01:30:30.968 --> 01:30:33.387
Manufactured products!

642
01:30:46.609 --> 01:30:48.986
Oh God! No!

643
01:30:49.070 --> 01:30:52.823
No!
I slept too long!
